 ## Changelog
 
+- 2026-10-25 (11): the immersive inventory in 3D: the cloth screen moves from the flat HUD into the world (**NOT b1.7.3**; written WITHOUT a Rust toolchain: not compiled, not run, not seen on a device; +6 tests in `world/pack.rs` (`the_cloth_is_the_layouts_shape_and_lies_with_the_player_at_its_bottom`, `the_camera_frames_the_cloth_from_its_players_side_and_centred`, `the_camera_glides_with_the_cloth`, `a_finger_lands_on_the_unit_it_is_over`, `a_tap_on_a_cube_is_that_cube_wherever_on_the_cloth`, `the_scene_fits_its_budget_and_the_stacks_come_up_one_by_one`), `a_touch_finds_its_slot_or_the_empty_cloth` now in cloth units; run `cargo test --lib pack` first). `Screen::click`, `SlotId` and the zones of `pack::layout` are untouched.
+    - Cloth: `LEN` is now `H * UNIT` = 1.16 (2.0 x 1.16 blocks, the layout's 400 x 232; a unit is 0.005 blocks). `Mat::at(x, y, h)` puts a cloth unit in the world (layout y = 0 is the far edge, the quick-select row is nearest the player).
+    - Camera: `Mat::rig(aspect)` is a pose 78 degrees down, 60 degrees tall, as near as keeps the four corners within 96% of the frame, the look-at point slid along the cloth until the top and bottom margins match (6 rounds). `Mat::glide` blends from the eye to it by `ease(t)` of the cloth, so it arrives as the cloth finishes spreading and goes back as it rolls up. `render_frame` swaps it into `self.camera` (like the third-person view; `pack_saved` puts the physical one back in `render`), zeroes the bob and hides the hand. The world keeps running.
+    - Touch: `Mat::ray` / `Mat::touch` shoot the finger at the plane `pack::REST` and give cloth units; `pack::slot_at` takes them (no more px). A cube stands up from that plane (far edge: the ray is 44 degrees up, a cube top is some 15 units off), so `pack::pick` first tests the cubes of the last frame's `pack_scene` as boxes (`hit_box`) and only then goes plane -> unit -> `slot_at`. `App::slot_under` calls `pick`; the toggles and the edge of the cloth use `touch`.
+    - Scene (`pack::scene` -> `Scene { flats, lays }`): flats are thin boxes (patches 0.04..0.046, frames, toggles, the selected quick slot's yellow ring, the arrow), lays are the stacks. A block with a cube's shape (`pack::is_cube`, = not `flat_icon`, the list `push_block_icon` had) is a small cube in its terrain tiles with the grass / leaf tints (5 faces, no bottom); everything else one two-sided flat quad (sprite, plant tile, or flat colour): no 16-layer extrusion. Each stack is lit by the cell above the cloth (`lit`) and has a contact shadow quad pushed after, lit `SHADOW_DIM` = 5 levels dimmer (a sprite's own image, offset; a cube's footprint in dark wool). `BOXES` in `render/items.rs` grew by `pack::BOXES` = 2 + 30 flats + 2 x 46 stacks = 124 boxes (about 110 KB of buffer).
+    - Animation: `pack_age` (seconds since the screen opened) brings the stacks up one by one, `STAGGER` 0.025 s apart, each growing and dropping in over `POP` 0.2 s; `pack_lift` (0.12 s) floats the cursor stack `LIFT` 0.12 blocks over the finger, `FLOAT` 24 units above it, its shadow moving out as it rises.
+    - Text stays HUD: `draw_pack` (now text only) projects zone labels, counts, wear bars (`push_overlay`, split out of `push_stack`), the toggles' numbers and the finger's tooltip from `Mat::at` through this frame's view-projection. The old dim, weave and stitching are gone.
+    - Not done, on purpose: item physics, throwing from the cloth into the world (a tap outside it still throws as before), saving the cloth; the camera ignores a low ceiling (inside a block you see the cloth through its back faces); the scene a touch reads is the previous frame's; the items vanish at once when the screen closes while the cloth rolls up; picks of flat things use one plane (`REST`).
+    - UNVERIFIED: that it compiles and the tests pass (`lit_by`, the `PackDraw` signature, `Mat4 * Vec4` in `fit_dist`), every number (78 degrees, 60 degrees, `FIT`, fills 0.78 / 0.95, `SHADOW_DIM`, the patch and frame colours), the look of the cube tiles and the shadows in both renderers, and that the far row is easy enough to hit.
 - 2026-10-25 (10): passive mobs spawn more often, counted around the player (**NOT b1.7.3**; `world/mobs.rs` was compiled and its 20 tests run in a Linux scratch crate (rustc 1.75, the `world` modules without `lib.rs`); the rest of mc-rs is not compiled; +1 test `mobs::tests::animals_refill_fast_never_crowd_and_keep_apart`; run `cargo test --lib mobs` first). Was: one pack (1..4 of a kind) every 400 ticks (20 s) at a point 24..48 blocks off, and only while the whole list held fewer than 12 animals, so a killed herd took 20 s and more to come back and a stray 100 blocks away held the refill.
